35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, the yard is a mess. Old scanners, spreadsheets everywhere. And we can’t stop work in winter. We need a system that fits this chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the invoices confirm my fear. Bundled prices stay flat, but separate add-ons climb yearly. We are buying a trap, not a system.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, your invoice data is critical. But my findings confirm the ownership gap. Last winter, four suppliers pointed fingers for two days. We need a single throat to choke.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that sounds scary! But I found the dispatch tool skipped three upgrades because testing took too long. And the 2018 pay move had bad data for a whole year!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your findings are sobering. I see two key administrators retiring, and supervisors quietly abandoning new routines. We must choose a path that respects their deep, hard-won knowledge.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, a single owner is vital. But with no winter freeze, how do we deploy without stopping freight? We need a plan that works around our calendar.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, the board minutes show capital gets cut, but operating costs pass easily. We are setting ourselves up for a perpetual, unchecked drain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, a single owner is vital. But my findings show the plan dies within months. Warehouse rules were rewritten twice. We need a system that absorbs change, not one that breaks it.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, that’s why we can’t just buy a box! If the data is messy, the system fails. We need someone who stays to fix the mess, not just install it!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the calendar is a wall, but the people are the bridge. We must choose a vendor who stays to teach, not one who leaves us stranded.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, you’re right. We need someone who stays. But @Asuka, if the plan drifts, how do we keep it honest?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the board minutes prove capital gets cut, but operating costs pass easily. We are setting ourselves up for a perpetual, unchecked drain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, we keep the plan honest by choosing a vendor who stays. If the scope drifts, we need a partner who adapts with us, not one who blames the business.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! If the data is messy, the system fails. We need someone who stays to fix the mess, not just install it!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right. A partner who stays is essential. But we must also honor the supervisors' routines. We cannot force change; we must guide it gently.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree. We need a team that stays to help us through the winter freeze. Can they work around our 24/7 schedule?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, staying is good, but I need to know if the price stays flat. I will check the renewal invoices to see if we are trapped in rising costs.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, staying is necessary, but I need to know if the scope holds. My findings show the plan dies within months. We need a partner who adapts, not one who blames the business.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, rising costs are bad, but messy data is worse! I saw the 2018 lift fail for a year. We need a vendor who stays to fix the mess, not just install it!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
