67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, on-site presence doesn't guarantee scope stability. My findings show plans drift regardless of vendor type. We need a partner who adapts to our changing rules, not just one who sits in the building.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, flat prices are nice, but I saw the 2018 data mess last! Anchor’s team stays to fix it. That’s what matters most!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right. Presence is not enough. We need a partner who respects the supervisors' deep routines, not one who forces a rigid template upon them.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, I worry about the old scanners. If Anchor’s team can’t make them talk to the new system, we’re stuck. Can they handle our mixed equipment?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the on-site team is a capital expense, which the board will likely trim. I need to see if their maintenance costs become an unchecked operating drain.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
